---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Objective</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    As a final-year Computer Science major with internship experience at Nokia and Microsoft (The Coalition), I am eager to apply my technical skills, knowledge, and passion for programming to
contribute to a challenging and dynamic environment as a full-time software engineer starting May 2027.
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Bachelor of Science Degree, Major in Computer Science"
      subtitle="University of British Columbia (UBC), Kelowna, BC, Canada (Expected Graduation - May, 2027) "
    >
      <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Dean's List: 2023, 2024, 2025</li>
      <li class="mb-6" style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Relevant Coursework: COSC 499 Capstone, COSC 310 Software Engineering, COSC 304 Introduction to Databases, COSC 320 Analysis of Algorithms, COSC 407 Intro to Parallel Computing, COSC 222 Data Structures, COSC 328 Introduction to Networks</li>
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Secondary Education"
      subtitle="The Emerald Heights International School, Indore, India"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
  <TimeLineElement
      title="Software Test Intern - Nokia"
      subtitle="Nokia (January 2026 - August 2026)"
    >
      <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Built and expanded automated test frameworks using Pytest and Mocha for Nokia NSP's IP/Optical Correlation platform, strengthening regression coverage for critical network management workflows.</li>

    <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Designed and implemented end-to-end and functional test scenarios to validate feature behavior, identify defects, and ensure software quality across releases.</li>

    <li class = 'mb-6' style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Created reusable automation components and debugging tools that improved test reliability, reduced development effort, and enabled faster validation of new product capabilities.</li>
    </TimeLineElement>
  <TimeLineElement
      title="Software Engineering Intern - Microsoft, The Coalition"
      subtitle="Microsoft, The Coalition (September 2025 - November 2025)"
    >
      <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Built a Mass Broadcast library in C#/.NET to execute large-scale player actions concurrently across existing microservices.</li>

    <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Leveraged Azure, Orleans, and PostgreSQL to enable scalable, reliable backend workflows for live multiplayer services.</li>

    <li class = 'mb-6' style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Unified Npgsql database metrics and delivered a single Grafana dashboard, improving observability and debugging across services.</li>
    </TimeLineElement>
  <TimeLineElement
      title="Game Developer - Beaver World"
      subtitle="Centre for Culture and Technology, UBC Okanagan (May 2025 - August 2025)"
    >
      <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Built mission systems, inventory management, and in-game notifications using Unity and C# to enhance gameplay
functionality in a 3D educational platform.</li>

    <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Built scalable gameplay systems with modular scripts and managed collaborative development using Unity Version
Control, streamlining team workflows and feature integration.</li>

    <li class = 'mb-6' style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;" >Designed user interfaces in Figma and conducted usability testing, reducing task completion time by 30% through HCI-
informed UI iterations.</li>
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Subject Tutor"
      subtitle="UBC Okanagan Supplemental Learning Hub (September 2024 - April 2025)"
    >
      <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Delivered 1-on-1 tutoring in Computer Science and Math using visual aids and analogies to clarify complex concepts.</li>
    
    <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Tailored study plans to individual learning styles, resulting in a 15% average grade improvement.</li>
    
    <li class = 'mb-6' style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;" >Tracked progress for 20+ students using session logs and feedback, adjusting teaching methods for better outcomes.</li>
    </TimeLineElement>
    
    
    
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Co-Founder and Vice President of Software"
      subtitle="Artificial Intelligence Club, UBC Okanagan (September 2023 – August 2025)"
    >
      <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Co-founded and scaled UBCO’s AI Club to 200+ members through events, coding sessions, and outreach initiatives.</li>
      <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Led development of an AI chatbot using Java, AIML, and NLP; hosted workshops on OOP design for student developers.</li>
      <li style="text-indent: -20px; padding-left: 20px;">Organized technical sessions with professors, boosting event attendance by 40% and enhancing peer learning.</li>
    </TimeLineElement>
    

  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Certifications</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    <li>
      <a href='https://www.udemy.com/share/103J8C3@Yal_JzNuHOOxJALF-5X8YxDsKsjzVMrPbC3J-5vwoDcYfY59fIVRS8OlyB9ShQdKVQ==/' target="_blank"> 100 Days of Code: The Complete Python Pro Bootcamp bu Angela Yu</a>
    </li>
    
    <li>
      <a href='https://www.udemy.com/share/101W923@zwFaYa73SksvOBS2OdQoztriZc1EwtTd8hJc3Upzvb2xZKsY49s2kkWZP3eXozPlLg==/' target="_blank"> Master the Coding Interviews: Data Structures and Algorithms by Andrei Neagoie</a>
    </li>

    <li>
      <a href="https://www.udemy.com/share/101W923@zwFaYa73SksvOBS2OdQoztriZc1EwtTd8hJc3Upzvb2xZKsY49s2kkWZP3eXozPlLg==/" target="_blank">The Web Developer Bootcamp 2024 by Colt Steele </a>
    </li>


    
  </ul>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Skills</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <div class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Programming Languages</div>
    <ul class="list-disc md:columns-5 columns-2 mx-6">
      <li>Python</li>
      <li>Java</li>
      <li>JavaScript</li>
      <li>TypeScript</li>
      <li>C++</li>
      <li>C#</li>
      <li>SQL</li>
      <li>Bash</li>
      <li>HTML/CSS</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <div class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Frameworks & Tools</div>
    <ul class="list-disc md:columns-5 columns-2 mx-6">
      <li>Node.js</li>
      <li>React</li>
      <li>Django</li>
      <li>Flask</li>
      <li>Express</li>
      <li>Unity</li>
      <li>Android Studio</li>
      <li>REST APIs</li>
      <li>Postman</li>
      <li>Mocha</li>
      <li>Jest / Testing Libraries</li>
      <li>Figma / UI Design</li>
      <li>MongoDB</li>
      <li>Firebase/Firestore</li>
      <li>PostgreSQL</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Cloud & DevOps</div>
    <ul class="list-disc md:columns-5 columns-2 mx-6">
      <li>Azure</li>
      <li>AWS (basic)</li>
      <li>Docker</li>
      <li>Kubernetes</li>
      <li>GitHub Actions</li>
      <li>CI/CD</li>
      <li>Git / Version Control</li>
      <li>Linux/Unix</li>
      <li>Agile/Scrum</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
